Reusable Workflows in GitHub Actions

Today I learned how reusable workflows help reduce duplication and standardize CI/CD pipelines.

🔹 workflow_call
workflow_call allows one workflow to:
Call another workflow
Pass inputs and secrets
Reuse common logic
This enables modular pipelines.

🔹 Sharing Workflows
Reusable workflows can be:
Shared across repositories
Maintained in a central repo
Version-controlled
This improves consistency.

🔹 DRY Principles
Reusable workflows follow DRY:
Don’t Repeat Yourself
Less duplication
Easier maintenance
Cleaner pipelines scale better.

🔥 3-Line Takeaway
Reuse reduces complexity.
 DRY improves consistency.
 Workflows scale better.
